			Johnston Engineering, PLLC

Johnston Engineering is pleased to submit this proposal in response to Capture6's Request for Proposal (RFP) for a Containerized Pilot system to capture Carbon Dioxide (CO2). Johnston Engineering has specific, relevant, and recent design, build, and test experience in containerized carbon capture and electrolytic processes.  We have expertise in systems integration and packaging, and a proven track record of collaboration with customer chemical engineering teams to accurately design and build systems for complex chemical processes that make us a strong fit for this project.

Johnston Engineering is proposing to lead the project with support from our control systems and software engineering subcontractor, InfoTech North Star (ITNS). Johnston Engineering will handle all mechanical engineering, procurement and commissioning tasks outlined in the budgetary cost proposal, as well as manage the overall project. ITNS will be responsible for all software engineering tasks, including software development and system controls, as detailed in the budgetary cost proposal.

This proposal document will provide a budgetary cost proposal of the design, build, test, and required documentation for the containerized pilot. Additionally, it highlights Johnston Engineering and InfoTech NorthStar’s qualifications, credentials, relevant project experience, and references to complete the work successfully. Please also review the accompanying “Johnston Engineering– Capture6: Tortuga Proposal” PowerPoint attached to this proposal, which further describes our relevant capabilities, expertise, and desire to undertake this project.  

This proposal is split into two main sections. Section 1 – Project Team, Capabilities and References and Section 2- Scope, Deliverables and budgetary pricing.  

