# Project Team, Capabilities, Projects and References

## Introduction to Johnston Engineering

Johnston Engineering (JE) is a mechanical engineering firm located in Spokane, Washington specializing in mechanical design, analysis, integration, build, and testing of first-of-a-kind systems, equipment, and machines. JE focuses on clean technology industries with over 80% of our revenue coming from carbon, hydrogen, nuclear, and energy storage technologies. 

Johnston Engineering's unique advantage is that we use an “Analysis-Driven Design” approach, meaning that we have a closely integrated mechanical design with physics-based simulations of thermal, structural, and fluid-flow analysis to optimize and validate designs before anything gets built – ensuring product performance and avoiding part failures. Utilizing SolidWorks 3D CAD and ANSYS analysis software, we excel in component modeling, analysis, and system integration. Our expertise includes performing Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) and Thermal and Structural Finite Element Analysis (FEA) to simulate the performance of mechanical hardware systems, considering forces, pressures, torques, temperature, and flow geometry. We then iterate design and analysis simulations until desired performance outcomes are achieved.

Johnston Engineering President, Andy Johnston, P.E., provides subject matter expertise in structural, thermal, and fluid analysis with over 20 years of experience in clean energy, military, and aerospace research, design, analysis, build, and test of first-of-a-kind systems. Johnston Engineering has completed over 150 projects, designing custom components and full systems, including Direct Air Capture (DAC) and Boiler Exhaust Carbon Capture systems, hydrogen systems, scaling up and testing electrolyzers and reformers, pulsed power demonstration units, advanced nuclear, and multiple LDES demonstration units. Our clients include National Labs, Start-Ups, and larger companies working on research & development of their innovative technologies. 

Johnston Engineering is headquartered in Washington State with over 160 years of combined engineering experience. In operation for 9 years, our total team is 29 individuals which includes 13 full-time technical staff of mechanical engineers and designers plus (3) support and fabrication staff, and (14) engineering contractors used for software and electrical engineering. 

## Introduction to InfoTech NorthStar (ITNS)

InfoTech NorthStar, LLC (ITNS) is a turnkey control system software engineering services company based in Richland, Washington. ITNS specializes in managing and executing complex projects with tight timelines, ensuring they are delivered on budget and within schedule while maintaining high-quality standards. ITNS’s expertise in systems control and monitoring has enabled the development and operation of over 30 active applications and control systems for commercial and government clients including within the DOE complex and its contractors. ITNS has extensive experience providing complex systems and collaborating with various engineering disciplines to integrate system components for testing and demonstration purposes

## Johnston Engineering Capabilities Most Relevant to Project Tortuga

Johnston Engineering has specific, relevant, and recent design, build, and test experience in containerized carbon capture and electrolytic processes, as well as expertise in systems integration and packaging, and a proven track record of collaboration with our client’s chemical engineering teams to accurately model and build systems for complex chemical processes.

Our core competencies that make us the ideal partner for this project include:

- Custom Containerized System and Component Design

- Custom mechanical hardware and component design, system layout, and packaging for containerized systems. 

- Proficiency in ANSYS structural Finite Element Analysis (FEA) and Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD).

- Structural Analysis

- Johnston Engineering’s team excels in conducting structural analysis ensuring components are properly mounted and capable of withstanding transportation acceleration loads. 

- Capable of conducting structural analysis for all components in Tortuga containerized system including tanks, BEPD, direct air contactor units, CSTR, and RO systems.

- Fluid Analysis

- Fluid distribution

- Vapor and liquid pressure drop

- Fabrication:

- We rely on a network of trusted local fabrication vendors for metal, plastic, and composite material fabrication. These relationships enable us to obtain parts quickly and at competitive prices. Additionally, we own a fully equipped fabrication shop with mills, lathes, sheet metal tools, and welding equipment, allowing us to expedite fabrication or make adjustments to delivered parts quickly. 

- Testing/ Commissioning:

- Design of custom test fixtures and data acquisition systems tailored to the specific requirements of experiments. This includes integrating sensors, instrumentation, and control systems.

- Conducting testing, data reduction, correlation development, and uncertainty analysis.

Please also review the accompanying Johnston Engineering Proposal – Capture6, which further describes our relevant capabilities, expertise, and desire to undertake this project. Links to further capability information regarding structural and fluid analysis can be found here - [https://www.johnstonpe.com/analysis-services](https://www.johnstonpe.com/analysis-services). 

